# The stage commands: one table that the engine's lists, the on-chain compiler's COMMANDS and the docs are checked
# against (docs/stage-driver.md § Command table). The dispatch in stage.cpp is still written by hand.
#
# One command a line:  NAME  KIND  MIN  WIN  TEXT  LIVE  | what it does
#   KIND  run: a timed line (@T NAME ...); head: a header line of the stage file (no time)
#   MIN   the fewest words after NAME, before any |text
#   WIN   y: the first word names a window that must be open (stage.cpp needWin[])
#   TEXT  y: the command takes |text after its words
#   LIVE  y: window.wwdosStage.run() accepts it (stage.cpp checkLive known[]); n: it refuses it (notLive[])
#
# name     kind min win text live | doc
clock      head 1   n   n    n    | ticks per second (default 8)
size       head 2   n   n    n    | the desktop the stage was laid out for, W H
open       run  5   n   y    y    | opens a window of a primer; on an open NAME it moves and retitles it
move       run  3   y   n    y    | glides the window to X Y [in S] [ease]
rect       run  5   y   n    y    | glides position and size; 0 0 is the primer's own size again
close      run  1   y   n    y    | closes the window
raise      run  1   y   n    y    | brings the window to the front
lower      run  1   y   n    y    | sends the window to the back
title      run  1   y   y    y    | retitles the window
swap       run  2   y   n    y    | new contents; place, title and depth stay
say        run  1   y   y    y    | a speech bubble above the window for S seconds (default 3)
hint       run  0   n   y    y    | the status line's right-hand text
bg         run  1   n   n    y    | the desktop pattern (a preset name)
theme      run  1   n   n    y    | the whole desktop's palette: ega or monochrome
colour     run  2   y   n    y    | one window's colour family and text ink
mark       run  2   n   n    y    | line art on the desktop under every window; mark NAME off removes it
weather    run  1   n   n    y    | rain, a lightning flash, or off
shake      run  0   n   n    y    | every stage window jitters for S seconds, seeded
seed       run  1   n   n    y    | the seed of everything random (shake); default 0
floors     run  1   n   n    y    | off: stage windows keep their sizes; on (default): Turbo Vision's 16x6 floor
tile       run  0   n   n    y    | Turbo Vision's tiled window layout
cascade    run  0   n   n    y    | Turbo Vision's cascaded window layout
bars       run  1   n   n    y    | shows or hides the menu bar and status line
sound      run  1   n   n    y    | plays the scene's clip NAME, or a synthesised effect ~NAME
drift      run  3   n   n    y    | the mark NAME moves VX cells a second right and VY down from now; drift NAME 0 0 stops it
text       run  1   y   y    y    | the window shows these lines (engine widget)
bar        run  5   y   n    y    | a progress bar filling from FROM to TO percent (engine widget)
counter    run  5   y   y    y    | a number running from FROM to TO in FORMAT's %d (engine widget)
scrubber   run  1   n   n    y    | the small timeline in the status line, or the wide one across the bottom two rows
gate       run  0   n   n    n    | holds the clock until the first click or key
section    run  0   n   y    n    | marks a part of the piece for PgDn, PgUp and the scrubbers
tempo      run  1   n   n    n    | bar 1 of the film starts here (written by the compiler from bpm)
loop       run  0   n   n    n    | clock back to T seconds (default 0)
end        run  0   n   n    n    | stops the clock
